  "goodToKnow": "Die Monarchie is a monarchy: eine konstitutionelle Monarchie, die Abschaffung der Monarchie. Germany's monarchies ended in November 1918, when Kaiser Wilhelm II abdicated and the republic was proclaimed; noble titles became part of surnames. European monarchies today include the UK, Spain, the Netherlands, Belgium, Sweden, Denmark, Norway and Liechtenstein. Der Monarch is the monarch. Stressed on the last syllable: mo-nar-KHEE."
